      "current_title": "Ask HN: What are some cool but obscure data structures you know about?",
      "excerpt": "I'm very interested in what types of interesting data structures are out there HN. Totally your preference. I'll start: bloom filters. Lets you test if a value is definitely NOT in a list of pre-stored values (or POSSIBLY in a list - with adjustable probability that influences storage of the values.) Good use-case: routing. Say you have a list of 1 million IPs that are black listed. A trivial algorithm would be to compare every element of the set with a given IP. The time com",
      "rank": 1,
      "guide_zh": "征集有趣却鲜为人知的数据结构及其用途。"
